FAQs:
&nbsp;
 Who is TMNT?
&nbsp;
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles are four fictional teenaged turtles named after Italian Renaissance artists. 
&nbsp;
 What were the turtles good at?
&nbsp;
The Ninja Turtles were trained to excel at the art of ninjutsu. At their home, in an attempt to remain hidden from the society they used to battle petty criminals, mutated creatures, and alien invaders. 
&nbsp;
 When did they make their first appearance?
&nbsp;
The characters first appeared in comic books and later took on to feature in cartoon series, video games, toys and other merchandise after they were appreciated and were loved by the readers of comic books.
 
 Why did the creators move on from live-action to animation?
&nbsp;
The prime reason was to try something different as live-action was already done. Also, it would have been insanely expensive to constantly produce live-action films and animation was tried and tested since it opens up to great expansions and you can do a lot of things without worrying about the expenses. 
&nbsp;
 Where do the turtles live?
&nbsp;
New York City, 
&nbsp;
 Since Ninja Turtles come under superheroes, are they from Marvel or DC?
&nbsp;
They are neither from Marvel nor from DC and were originally owned by Mirage comics. 
&nbsp;
 Is there a girl Ninja Turtle?
&nbsp;
Venus Di Milo is a female Ninja Turtle within the franchise and she first appeared in the series Ninja Turtles: The Next Mutation. She was portrayed by Nicole Parker and the voice behind her was the melodious Lalainia Lindbjerg.

